WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.435
-My first guest is an Oscar-,

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.435
Tony-, Emmy-,

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.571
and Golden Globe-winning
actress,

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:09.008
starring in the highly acclaimed
film "Ma Rainey's Black Bottom,"

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.177
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.147
Here is the very talented
Viola Davis!

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.515
[ Band plays funk ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.250
Yeah, Viola Davis!

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.319
Oh, I love you!

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.321
Welcome back.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.190
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.357
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:26.493
Thank you so much
for doing this.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:27.860
I appreciate it.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.029
-Oh, my goodness. [ Laughs ]
-It's great to see you.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.532
I want to talk
about your Oscar nomination

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:36.602
in "Ma Rainey's Black Bottom,"
but I want to quickly touch on

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.005
you have a new addition
to your family.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.139
-I do.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.241
-A son.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.176
-Congratulations.
A son.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.745
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah.
-Here's a picture.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.913
Here's a picture.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.714
There. Awww!

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.449
-Awww!
-That's so cute.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:51.884
Are you kidding me?
-Bailey.

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:55.021
-Bailey?
-Bailey is his name.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.957
-Whose idea was it
to get Bailey?

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.592
-Well, let me tell you
something.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.361
-[ Laughing ]
That is a story.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.095
Whose idea it was,

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.564
was my husband.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.766
[ Laughter ]
My husband, of all people.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.568
You know,
I married George Jefferson.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.536
[ Laughter ]
I fell in love with my husband

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:13.072
because I saw a baseball bat
near his bed

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.074
and I said, "I love him."

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.277
He's like my father, you know?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.577
And he was like,
"We ain't never getting

00:01:18.577 --> 00:01:20.045
no damn dog in this house.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:21.514
They tear up the yard.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.816
They piss all over the place.
Fur."

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.152
And then, cut to this morning.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.688
I'm listening to him
downstairs, going,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.955
"Hey, my Bailey boo.

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.357
[ Laughter and applause ]
I love you.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.625
Daddy is here.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.860
You my baby."

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.860
So there you go.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.996
[ Laughter ]
-I love it.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.764
You know, the Internet
was going crazy today

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:42.568
because the "Suicide Squad"
trailer was released.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.403
Congrats on that.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.772
It's major.
-Thank you.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:49.008
[ Cheering and applause ]
-That's going to be giant.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:52.144
You tweeted it out
and James Gunn had a response,

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:55.615
said, "No lie, @violadavis is
so scary as Amanda Waller,

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.917
I was afraid to give her
acting notes on set."

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.219
[ Laughter ]
-That's right.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.288
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:06.025
I channeled my inner child,
Jimmy.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.293
-Really?
-Because, when I was a kid,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:10.663
I was real tough,
but I really am not that tough.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.566
I mean, I appreciate
what James Gunn says,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.335
but that's one of the reasons
why I love playing that role,

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:20.506
because I get to cuss someone
like Idris Elba out, you know?

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.375
[ Laughter ]
-[ Claps ]

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.776
I also saw that you're going

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.178
to be playing Michelle Obama

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.180
in --
-Whoo!

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.914
-Yeah.
This is a big deal.

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:31.584
[ Cheering and applause ]
It's a new series.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.686
-Yeah.
-Why would you do this here?

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.789
You have
to keep testing yourself?

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.292
-I don't know. I think it was
temporary insanity.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.726
-[ Laughs, claps ]
I lost my damn mind

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.461
for about five minutes

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.964
and made a damn decision
that I can't take back.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:48.968
-Yeah.
-Because the woman is a goddess

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.471
-Yeah.
-and everybody knows her.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.572
[ Cheering and applause ]
Everybody feels like

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:57.142
they want to protect her.

00:02:57.142 --> 00:02:59.511
Here's the thing -- I'm just
going to do the best I can.

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:00.546
-[ Laughs ]
-That's what I say

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:01.680
to my daughter every morning.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.282
I said, "Genesis,
let me tell you something.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.584
Mommy is doing the best
she can," so that's it.

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:09.188
-That's exactly right.
That's exactly right.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:12.692
Have you talked to Michelle
since they announced this?

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.193
-Oh, yes, I have.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.294
-Yeah? Good.
-I have.

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:17.130
For several hours.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.466
And it's terrifying
because she's --

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.733
Here's the thing.

00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:25.138
Sometimes someone
doesn't live up

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.673
to whatever image
you have in your head,

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.677
but when they do live up to the
image, it's quite frightening.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.478
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah! [ Claps ]
-You know?

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.747
It really is.
-She really does live up to --

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.449
She actually is that cool
and that awesome.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.118
You're going to knock it
out of the park.
-Yeah, she's that cool, yeah.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.387
-I love "Ma Rainey's
Black Bottom."

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.022
I thought you were fantastic...
-Thank you.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:46.192
-...unrecognizable, almost,
in this film.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.795
-Thank you.
-You had all this weight gain.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.063
You had the hair

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.699
and...the teeth.
-The grilles. My grilles.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.134
-Oh, my gosh!
-Making my grille.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.869
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:57.970
You were unbelievable.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.939
-Congrats on that
-Thank you.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.206
-nomination.

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:04.076
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:05.978
It's a great story.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:08.781
Ma Rainey is also known
as the Mother of the Blues.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.217
-Yes.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:16.355
-It puts you in the Roaring '20s
and in Chicago, exactly.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.124
They did such a great job
with that.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.593
And, obviously,
Chadwick Boseman as well

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.461
is in the film.
-Absolutely.

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:24.630
Awesome, Chadwick Boseman.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.632
And, you know, I told Ann Roth

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:30.269
that I wanted a body like
Aretha Franklin.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:33.372
So I sent her a picture
of Aretha Franklin.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.775
I said, "I want my body
to look like that."

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:39.745
-Yeah.
-And so she built me a padding

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:41.247
and I'm telling you,

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.816
I never felt sexier.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.850
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Is that right?
-No.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.685
-Wow!
-I felt like my Aunt Joyce.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.054
Jimmy, I had
an Aunt Joyce growing up.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:51.223
Aunt Joyce was beautiful to me.

00:04:51.223 --> 00:04:52.692
She was over 300 pounds.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.660
She wore the latest fashions

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.196
and you could not tell
that woman she wasn't cute.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.964
She didn't have any problems
getting a man,

00:04:58.964 --> 00:05:00.733
keeping a man, nothing.
-[ Claps ]

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.302
[ Cheering and applause ]
-So, when I put on that padding,

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.470
I felt cute!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.538
[ Laughter ]
-You were, oh!

00:05:06.538 --> 00:05:07.540
You were great.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.141
For anyone who hasn't seen it,

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:11.544
can you set up
what the movie's about?

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:15.181
-Well, this movie literally
is very, very simple.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.449
This is the Mother of the Blues,
Ma Rainey,

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:22.021
who is in Chicago to record
an album with her band.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:25.091
And this is a day in the life
of recording that album

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.727
and everything
that she has to fight,

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:31.330
from the time she walks into the
studio to the time she leaves,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.598
and that is it.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.801
-Yeah.
I think, you know,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.969
you're amazing
in everything you do.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:40.973
I'm a big fan, but I also like
Chadwick as well because he

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:43.543
-Oh, awesome. Beautiful.
-created this character

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:46.879
and you go, "Oh, that's a really
interesting way to play that."

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.048
-Yeah, it is, you know.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:52.117
This is someone who's just
running from trauma, you know,

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:54.353
and probably someone
with all the talent

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.654
and vision in the world,

00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:58.457
but doesn't understand that,
you know,

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.759
you can't reconcile the past.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:01.827
You know, you have to see it.

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:03.762
It's just a heartbreaking
performance.

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:06.833
And, you know, the thing --
I just --

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.569
you know, I always say
I wish for everyone

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:14.307
that they could have just spent
a minute with Chadwick Boseman.

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.541
He was everything.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.477
Like I said, not everyone
lives up to their name,

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:23.916
but this young man, he lived up
to his name and his reputation.

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.619
He was a beautiful human being.
-Ah.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.921
[ Applause ]
I want to show --

00:06:29.921 --> 00:06:31.190
I want to show a clip.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.026
Here's Viola Davis
in "Ma Rainey's Black Bottom."

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.027
Take a look.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.295
-Damn what the band say.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.230
You supposed to have
my Coca-Cola. You knew that.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.331
-[ Laughs ]
-I ain't doing nothing

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:40.700
without my Coca-Cola.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:43.035
-Just a minute, here, Ma.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:44.203
You come in an hour late --

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:45.337
-You need to get
out my face, Irvin.

00:06:45.337 --> 00:06:46.405
I told you,
keep him away from me.

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.473
-Mel, I'm tired of her nonsense.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:48.574
I'm not going
to put up with this.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.642
-Let me.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.909
Ma, listen.

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:52.478
I'll call down to the deli
and I'll get a Coke,

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.112
but let's get started, huh?

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:55.847
Sylvester's standing there,
ready to go.

00:06:55.847 --> 00:06:57.116
The band's all set up.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.417
Let's do this one song, huh?

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:00.653
-Too cheap to buy me
a Coca-Cola, I'll buy my own.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:02.988
Slow Drag, Sylvester.
Come on, baby.

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:05.657
Get me three bottles
of Coca-Cola, ice-cold.

00:07:05.657 --> 00:07:07.393
Get y'all something, too.
Keep the change.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:08.827
-Yes, ma'am.

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:10.663
-Irvin, get away from me!

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:12.298
You can wait 'til I get
my Coca-Cola.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.000
Ain't gonna kill you.
-Okay, Ma.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.435
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Get the Coca Cola!

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:17.569
Who was that?!
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:19.839
-Who was it?
-You know, Jimmy, though,

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:22.241
you know it wasn't really
about the Coca-Cola.

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:23.743
-No, I know, exactly,
right, yeah.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.311
-[ Laughs ]
-Oh, my gosh. You're amazing.

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:27.112
Viola Davis, everybody.
Thank you so much

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:28.881
for coming out.
-Thank you.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:30.549
Thank you, Jimmy.
-Say hi to Bailey!

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:32.718
"Ma Rainey's Black Bottom"
is on Netflix, everybody.

